# Testing & Benchmarks

## Coverage
- Every public SQL function MUST have at least one Pytest assertion covering happy path.
- Critical paths (ledger integrity, RLS, Monte Carlo invariants) require negative/edge tests.

## Performance Budgets
- Individual Pytest cases SHOULD complete in under 5 seconds (excluding one-time schema bootstrap).
- Benchmarks MUST report p95 latency.
- Decision batch processing p95 target: < 200ms per item on local Docker Postgres for seed-scale data.

## Fixtures
- Use `db_connection`, `setup_schema`, `seed_data`, and `tenant_context` from `conftest.py`.
- Override clock with `SET cardops.mock_now = '...'` when asserting temporal behavior.

## CI Expectations
- Order: lint-sql → test → smoke → benchmark.
- Fail CI on any integrity or RLS leakage failure.
